      "comment": "SPANISH ARMADA (2) is the clear top pick after going within a neck of Juniper in a CL1 at Belmont, with that mid-week form looking the strongest recent reference among the main chances. His record around 1200m is sound, he is race fit, and the 2kg claim helps him present as the runner with the most reliable winning case. ESPINHO (5) has to be forgiven for a plain Bunbury result when last in a CL3, but he is third-up, suited at 1200m and his previous Belmont fifth had more merit than the finishing position suggests. DIEGO DYNAMITE (7) brings consecutive CL3 placings and has been competitive at generous odds, so he is a genuine danger with proven 1200m form. VILLAGE GIRL (3) is eased from Saturday company after finishing within four and a half lengths in a 3yo+ Open, and her depth of 1200m experience keeps her in the wider winning mix if she sharpens late. BACKCHATTING (8) can be in the finish on resumption.",
